{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00437",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.18,
      "end_seconds": 6.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.65,
      "end_seconds": 12.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.86,
      "end_seconds": 19.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out. I mean, we came because of diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.34,
      "end_seconds": 22.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.09,
      "end_seconds": 30.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.86,
      "text": "Hmm, it's been two weeks, I'm fairly sure. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.23,
      "end_seconds": 35.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Is it constant, or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.14,
      "end_seconds": 39.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Um, it sort of comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.14,
      "end_seconds": 42.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.56,
      "end_seconds": 47.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Okay, so it usually comes with a low fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.12,
      "end_seconds": 49.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Any stomach cramps as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.61,
      "end_seconds": 54.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Yeah. One week, you know, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.65,
      "end_seconds": 57.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "What's the pattern, is it there all day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.33,
      "end_seconds": 70.7,
      "duration_seconds": 12.37,
      "text": "It's, It's all the time. Um, the low fever? That's been for three days. Yeah, as for low fever, it just comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.7,
      "end_seconds": 73.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "So, have you had nausea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.37,
      "end_seconds": 80.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, yes, since last Tuesday. With nausea, pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.8,
      "end_seconds": 95.94,
      "duration_seconds": 14.14,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.56,
      "end_seconds": 102.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Yeah, okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.75,
      "end_seconds": 104.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Any vomiting or recent antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.96,
      "end_seconds": 111.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "No vomiting or recent antibiotics, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.3,
      "end_seconds": 115.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Any rash, weight loss or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.65,
      "end_seconds": 119.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "No, no rash, weight loss or black stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.51,
      "end_seconds": 123.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.25,
      "end_seconds": 126.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Oh, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 128.13,
      "end_seconds": 136.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.15,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Heart rate 101, saturation 96 percent, temp 38.5 degrees. Blood pressure 125 over 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.2,
      "end_seconds": 141.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Good, thank you. What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.79,
      "end_seconds": 154.09,
      "duration_seconds": 11.3,
      "text": "I, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, you know, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.67,
      "end_seconds": 157.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Right, I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.16,
      "end_seconds": 159.05,
      "duration_seconds": 0.89,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.9,
      "end_seconds": 178.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.07,
      "end_seconds": 183.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Yes, I had cataract surgery on my right eye, last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.42,
      "end_seconds": 186.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.75,
      "end_seconds": 189.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.56,
      "end_seconds": 208.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.48,
      "end_seconds": 223.77,
      "duration_seconds": 14.29,
      "text": "Well, I have diabetes, for two years. I took the morning off to come in today. I've had arthritis in my knees, yes. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.99,
      "end_seconds": 238.43,
      "duration_seconds": 13.44,
      "text": "Yes, I can see the diabetes in your file as well. Right, so that's your known arthritis in my knees. We'll keep that in mind today. Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.49,
      "end_seconds": 250.99,
      "duration_seconds": 11.5,
      "text": "Um, I take glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar. Well, it's paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed for the knee pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 251.67,
      "end_seconds": 255.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 1300 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.31,
      "end_seconds": 261.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.87,
      "end_seconds": 268.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "No, I left it at home. It's ORS, a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.02,
      "end_seconds": 272.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.02,
      "end_seconds": 273.72,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.44,
      "end_seconds": 286.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.61,
      "end_seconds": 292.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.83,
      "end_seconds": 296.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.05,
      "end_seconds": 313.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Bowel sounds are active, tummy is soft with mild tenderness all around."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.75,
      "end_seconds": 316.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Hold your arm out like this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.78,
      "end_seconds": 336.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "You're mildly dehydrated."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.04,
      "end_seconds": 370.78,
      "duration_seconds": 28.74,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is acute gastroenteritis. I'd also keep an infective colitis in mind. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had diarrhoea for two weeks, and no recent antibiotics or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.72,
      "end_seconds": 373.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.98,
      "end_seconds": 398.95,
      "duration_seconds": 24.97,
      "text": "Let's get a stool test, for diarrhoea. I'm going to order blood salts, for dehydration. Let's use zinc, 20 milligrams, once a day, for ten days. That's for diarrhoea. Stick to bananas, rice, toast, curd, and avoid milk and oily food till it settles. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.08,
      "end_seconds": 406.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 408.0,
      "end_seconds": 409.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 409.83,
      "end_seconds": 417.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "If you pass blood or can't keep anything down, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 418.2,
      "end_seconds": 421.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Got it, um, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.71,
      "end_seconds": 431.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.83,
      "text": "Please come and see me if it's not better in three days. I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 431.9,
      "end_seconds": 444.24,
      "duration_seconds": 12.34,
      "text": "So, um, I take the zinc, 20 milligrams, once a day and come back if it's not better in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 445.18,
      "end_seconds": 449.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we've covered it. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 450.78,
      "end_seconds": 453.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Thanks so much, uh, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 454.99,
      "end_seconds": 456.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}